[OPEN] Binding Circle undead are just way too strong. They trivialize everything when summoned by a high level necromancer. We need to figure out how to balance them. Again, give me some IDEAS here and not just an immediate fix. Let’s brainstorm this.
    [ANSWERED] See "Design Notes: Readability and the Binding Circle.md".
    Short version: `craftUndead` pours ONE linear uncapped scalar into every stat —
    m = magic x (necromancy ? 1.5 : 1) — so at magic 100 a Bone Knight arrives with
    atk 96, def 48, tough 160 for 2 remains and 16 mana, and a lich mints m=225
    bodies. There is a cap of 15 (25 for a lich), and the risen DO NOT EAT: every
    existing pressure (bindStrain, host noise, materials) is a cost of BUILDING a
    host and none is a cost of HAVING one. Recommendation is upkeep first (gives the
    corpse economy a sink and self-corrects a bloated host), then splitting the flat
    1.5 Necromancy multiplier, then bending the stat curve last.

